I did think once about deliberately giving abusers bad bones files but 
rejected it.  If I angered them with bad bones files or pointlessly 
tried to prevent them from using the system I would be inviting 
retaliatory hack attempts against the server.  I don't have the time, 
the inclination, or the resources to deal with that sort of thing and it 
would probably mean the end of Hearse.

It's simpler just to cordon them off from other users.  Bones files 
expire after a certain number of downloads, but the bones that blocked 
users get don't count towards that.  So as far as everyone else is 
concerned they're having no effect on the system and may as well not 
exist.


